# Published benchmark sets whose doppler_meta.commit can never be put on main.
# Read by scripts/check_bench_commits.py (make bench-commits-check, #1322).
#
# One line per exempt (set, commit) PAIR, then why it cannot be fixed. A file
# in an exempt set passes only if its stamp IS the exempt commit: a new file
# there with any other off-main stamp fails, and re-stamping an exempt file
# fails while its old pair goes stale. This list may only SHRINK: the gate
# fails on an ADDED pair, on a pair no file fails with any more, and on a
# set whose directory is gone.
# A new set never goes here -- measure on main, or
# `make bench-restamp VERSION=...` it onto main's tree-identical commit.
v0.56.0 c9dbcf8da the commit is gone from GitHub (fetch answers "not our ref"), so its tree cannot be matched to a main commit
v0.57.0 5b444f08f measured on a tree that no commit on main has, so there is no identical commit to restamp to
